      "text": "1. Start by finding the prime factorization of each number.\n   - Prime factorization of 1407:\n     \\[\n     1407 \\div 3 = 469, \\quad 469 \\div 7 = 67\n     \\]\n   - Prime factorization of 67 is a prime number, so we can't continue factoring.\n\n   - Prime factorization of 903:\n     \\[\n     903 \\div 3 = 301, \\quad 301 \\div 7 = 43\n     \\]\n   - Prime factorization of 43 is a prime number, so we can't continue factoring.\n\n2. Now, determine the GCD by identifying the common prime factors.\n   - The prime factors of 1407 is 3, 7, and 67.\n   - The prime factors of 903 are 3 and 7.\n\n3. Using the prime factors with the greatest capacity, we get the GCD.\n   - The common prime factors are 3 and 7. The lowest power of 3 is 1 and of 7 is 1.\n\n4. Therefore, the greatest common divisor is 3 \\times 7 = 21.\n\n$\\boxed{21}$",
