      "text": "One method to find the greatest common divisor (GCD) of 1407 and 903 is as follows:\n\nStep 1: List the factors of each number.\n- Prime factorization of 1407: 1407 has 5 prime factors: 3, 11, 17, 19.\n- Prime factorization of 903: 903 has 7 prime factors: 3, 7, 11, 13.\n\nStep 2: Identify the shared prime factors.\n- The shared prime factors among 1407 and 903 are 3, 11, and 13.\n\nStep 3: Calculate the product of these shared prime factors.\n- The product of the shared prime factors is 3 * 11 * 13 = 429.\n\nThus, the greatest common divisor of 1407 and 903 is \\boxed{429}.",
