      "text": "Step 1: We start by finding the prime factorization of each number. \n\nPrime factorization is the process of breaking down a positive integer into a product of prime numbers.\n\nCase 1: The prime factorization of 1407\n1407 = 3 × 469 = 3 × 11 × 42 = 3 × 11 × 2 × 21 = 3 × 11 × 2 × 3 × 7 = 3 × 3 × 11 × 2 × 7 = 3 × 3 × 11 × 7.\nHence, the prime factorization of 1407 is \n$$1407 = 3^2\\times 11 \\times 7$$\nCase 2: The prime factorization of 903\n903 = 3 × 301 = 3 × 7 × 43.\nHence, the prime factorization of 903 is\n$$903 = 3 \\times 7.$$\n\n\nStep 2: Next, we create the the prime factors unique to each number.\n\nBecause we must have a nontrivial common divisor between the two numbers, there is at least one prime between the primes in each other's factorization.\n\nSo, the primer factors unique to each number are:\n\n$$3 \\quad \\text{ and } \\quad 7$$\nNext, by multiplying these primes we will get the greatest common divisor\n\n$$\\boxed{21}$$",
